-- title:
--   Mod p base change of the tangent–cusp form dictionary
-- statement:
--   Fix $N\ge 1$ and a prime $p$, and let $R=\mathtt{ratLocalizedAt}\ p$ be the subring of $\mathbb{Q}$ of rationals whose denominator is coprime to $p$. Let $c\colon X\to\operatorname{Spec}R$ be proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral, with a section $\varepsilon$ of $c$, and let $D$ consist of a scheme together with a structure morphism $D.\mathtt{toBase}$ to $\operatorname{Spec}R$ and a zero section; assume $hD$ says that $D$ represents, via a Poincaré rigidified line bundle with the universal property of `RepresentsRelSubPic`, the cut of the relative Picard functor of $c$ by fibrewise algebraic equivalence to zero, and that $D.\mathtt{toBase}$ is smooth and proper. Let $\mathcal V$ be a cover of $X$ by two affine opens with affine intersection, and let $\varphi$ assign to each element $t$ of $\mathtt{HeckeAlg}=\mathbb{Z}[x_\ell:\ell\text{ prime}]$ an endomorphism of $D$ over $\operatorname{Spec}R$ which, on $T$-valued points for every $T$, is a homomorphism for the relative group law $L$ attached to $hD$. Let $A$ be a commutative $R$-algebra whose structure map is surjective with kernel the ideal generated by $p$. Write, for an $R$-algebra $B$, $\Lambda(B)$ for the set of morphisms $\operatorname{Spec}B[\epsilon]\to D$ over $\operatorname{Spec}R$ whose composite with the reduction $\operatorname{Spec}B\to\operatorname{Spec}B[\epsilon]$ induced by $B[\epsilon]\to B$ is the unit section of $L$, and give the lattice $S=\mathtt{intLattice}\ N\ 2$ of weight-two cusp forms for $\Gamma_0(N)$ spanned by those with integral $q$-coefficients the $\mathtt{HeckeAlg}$-module structure of $\mathtt{latticeHeckeFamily}\ N$. The assertion: for every bijection $\tau\colon\Lambda(R)\to\operatorname{Hom}(S,R)$ (additive maps) such that $z=L.\mathrm{mul}\,x\,y$ implies $\tau z=\tau x+\tau y$, and such that $y=x$ followed by $\varphi t$ implies $\tau y(g)=\tau x(t\cdot g)$ for all $g\in S$, there exists a bijection $\tau_A\colon\Lambda(A)\to\operatorname{Hom}(S,A)$ which (1) is additive for $L$ in the same sense, (2) is compatible with base change: for every ring homomorphism $\beta\colon R[\epsilon]\to A[\epsilon]$ lying over the structure maps from $R$ and sending $\epsilon$ to $\epsilon$, and all $x\in\Lambda(R)$, $x_A\in\Lambda(A)$ with $x_A$ equal to $\operatorname{Spec}\beta$ followed by $x$, one has $\tau_A x_A(g)=$ the image of $\tau x(g)$ in $A$ for all $g\in S$, and (3) satisfies the same Hecke rule, $\tau_A y(g)=\tau_A x(t\cdot g)$ whenever $y$ is $x$ followed by $\varphi t$.
--
--   This is the descent, along $R\to R/(p)$, of the Hecke-equivariant identification of the tangent space at the identity of the relative Jacobian of $X/R$ with the dual of the integral lattice of weight-two cusp forms, phrased throughout in terms of dual-number points of the representing scheme of the relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ cut. It feeds the comparison of the mod $p$ cotangent space of the Jacobian model with $S_2(\Gamma_0(N);\mathbb{Z})\otimes A$ used in [`ModularCurve.exists_linearEquiv_baseChange_cotangent_model_jZero_torsion_tensor_intLattice_comp_mapCotangent_eq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_linearEquiv_baseChange_cotangent_model_jZero_torsion_tensor_intLattice_comp_mapCotangent_eq).
